	As a long-time science-fiction/fanzine fan, I'm used to having and
enjoying purely verbal relationships.  The idea that there is
"information" to be gotten from touching people is one that I've
heard from too many people I respect to find nonsensical, but my
imagination does not extend to what sort of information that might
be.

	On the other hand, I've recently joined a group where
hugging is all but mandatory, and to my surprise I find that I like that, too.

	I would guess that there'll be a wide range of approaches to
physical contact, just as there are now (perhaps wider, as there are more
possibilities).

